WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.310
Cool Kurusu!

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:03.980
Cheer me on!

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:06.570
Go for it, Anne-chan!

00:00:06.570 --> 00:00:08.500
Cool Kurusu!

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:14.140
Ready.

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:31.670
Anne-chan!

00:00:33.810 --> 00:00:35.760
Man, she really is amazing.

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:38.010
<i>Cool Kurusu!</i>

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:40.600
<i>Nice, Anne-chan!</i>

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:42.770
<i>Thanks-kurusu!</i>

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:45.770
Awesome.

00:00:45.770 --> 00:00:46.910
Isn't she?

00:00:46.910 --> 00:00:50.160
That's Kurusu Anne-chan, 
the Climbing Princess.

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:51.520
"Princess"?

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:54.920
She's a high schooler, like us, but she's a pro.

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:59.610
She's won several international competitions,
making her the sport's wunderkind.

00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:02.970
She's climbing's #1 heartthrob! 
How I want to be her!

00:01:02.970 --> 00:01:04.710
You want to be <i>that?</i>

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:06.960
Well, she is highly skilled.

00:01:07.910 --> 00:01:09.280
That she is.

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:12.560
Anyway, we have the Spring 
Climbing Championships tomorrow.

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:14.840
Let's do our best to bring 
it home for Hanamiya.

00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:16.010
Yeah!

00:01:18.190 --> 00:01:19.780
Am I going deaf? I can't hear you.

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:22.200
Let's do this thing!

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:23.420
Y-Yeah...

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:24.980
Yeah, let's do it.

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:47.620
<b><i>Iwakakeru!</i></b>

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:58.400
<b><i>Wall 2          Believe in Yourself</i></b>

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:05.550
Welcome to the Chiba Spring 
Climbing Championships.

00:03:05.550 --> 00:03:07.690
Today, we have the lead competition.

00:03:07.690 --> 00:03:08.660
There they are.

00:03:10.550 --> 00:03:12.840
This is your first competition, isn't it?

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:16.560
No need to be afraid.

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:18.750
Everyone here is a 
bird of the same feather.

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:22.280
But you... You seem different.

00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:26.200
I get the feeling you'll be very amusing.

00:03:27.320 --> 00:03:29.350
Don't be nervous, now.

00:03:29.350 --> 00:03:31.310
Hey, Iwamine!

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:33.260
Keep your legs off our newbie!

00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:37.510
It's been too long, Nono-chan. 
I'm glad to see you're as cute as ever.

00:03:37.510 --> 00:03:41.170
Did you get the 
wrong address, Iwamine-san?

00:03:41.170 --> 00:03:43.700
I'm pretty sure Kurikawa High
 isn't in this region.

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:46.880
Oh, this is very much the right place.

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:52.580
I'm here to see the oh-so-adorable 
looks on your faces when you fall.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:57.040
Too bad for you! I'm gonna 
send everything in my way!

00:03:57.040 --> 00:03:58.830
I wouldn't mind that, either.

00:03:58.830 --> 00:04:02.190
I love seeing your face 
overcome with joy, too.

00:04:02.190 --> 00:04:03.160
Toodles.

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:04.590
<i>I</i> never wanna see your face again!

00:04:04.970 --> 00:04:07.360
Who was that, Jun-chan?

00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:10.840
Iwamine Chinari. Runner-up in lead 
at the All-Japan Invitationals last year.

00:04:10.840 --> 00:04:13.640
Wait, <i>her?!</i> Number Two in Japan?

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:16.430
Yeah, her. Her skill is the real deal.

00:04:16.430 --> 00:04:18.960
By the way, the captain was the winner.

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:20.620
What? Wow!

00:04:20.620 --> 00:04:23.210
A-And I'm on her team?

00:04:23.210 --> 00:04:25.360
I'm starting to get even more nervous...

00:04:23.970 --> 00:04:25.360
You'll be fine!

00:04:25.630 --> 00:04:28.190
Just relax and leave everything to us.

00:04:28.190 --> 00:04:30.520
Hanamiya is unmatched in this zone.

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:33.150
Our captain is the reigning individual champion,

00:04:33.150 --> 00:04:35.120
and Nono-senpai was the runner-up.

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:37.130
It was a one-two finish for Hanamiya?

00:04:37.480 --> 00:04:40.060
Individual goes without saying,

00:04:40.060 --> 00:04:42.630
but we're also looking to be 
the champion team this year.

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:44.630
The champion team...

00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:46.970
We were the only members last year.

00:04:46.970 --> 00:04:49.130
Even a one-two finish wasn't enough.

00:04:49.130 --> 00:04:54.560
Team rankings are based on the 
top three individual scores.

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:56.660
And this year, we have four members!

00:04:57.510 --> 00:05:00.070
Of course, that means your result 
 will matter a lot, Konomi-san.

00:05:00.070 --> 00:05:02.090
My result matters?

00:05:02.090 --> 00:05:05.070
Konomin, you'll be fine 
as long as you observe.

00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:08.720
What route will you take? 
Which moves will you use?

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:12.950
Making the right game plan 
will make all the difference.

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:15.820
Uh, I only climbed for the 
first time yesterday...

00:05:15.820 --> 00:05:20.190
Jun's absolutely right.
 Top climbers conquer walls twice.

00:05:20.190 --> 00:05:23.300
Once on sight, and once with their bodies.

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:25.050
You can do it, Konomin.

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:26.300
Konomi-san?

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:27.550
Konomi-san!

00:05:27.980 --> 00:05:29.430
Let's enjoy this, okay?

00:05:29.810 --> 00:05:32.430
O-Okay...

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:33.440
Hang in there!

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:35.930
<b>Zonal High School 
Spring Climbing
 Championships</b>

00:05:33.440 --> 00:05:35.120
Like I told you yesterday,

00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:39.710
lead climbing involves clipping ropes 
into carabiners anchored to the wall.

00:05:39.710 --> 00:05:43.600
We're competing on how high we can 
go within the allotted time, right?

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:46.970
Yeah. The prelims have two problems: A and B.

00:05:46.970 --> 00:05:49.460
The time limit is six minutes each.

00:05:49.460 --> 00:05:51.520
If you fall, you're done.

00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:53.560
No retries, huh?

00:05:53.560 --> 00:05:54.780
Nono-senpai's up.

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:57.950
Next up is the first climber 
from the powerhouse Hanamiya Girls',

00:05:57.950 --> 00:05:59.680
Sugiura Nonoka!

00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:01.960
She's starting the prelims with Problem B.

00:06:02.270 --> 00:06:05.460
Watch her attempt closely.

00:06:11.790 --> 00:06:13.150
Say, Jun-chan.

00:06:13.150 --> 00:06:15.470
Don't shorter people have 
a disadvantage in climbing?

00:06:17.890 --> 00:06:22.980
They do, but they can compete just fine 
if they have something to cancel it out.

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:32.700
Whoo! A pied à main makes 
the hip joint feel so good!

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:33.710
Now...

00:06:33.710 --> 00:06:37.800
Flexibility is one of the most important 
traits you can have in climbing.

00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:41.000
Having a supple body 
opens up a lot of options.

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:44.000
Flexy Nonoka explodes up the wall!

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:46.020
How d'ya like that?

00:06:46.480 --> 00:06:49.150
Sugiura successfully sends Prelim Problem B!

00:06:49.150 --> 00:06:51.070
Wow, Nono-san!

00:06:50.480 --> 00:06:52.890
Meanwhile, last year's champion,

00:06:51.070 --> 00:06:52.890
Captain's starting with Problem A.

00:06:52.890 --> 00:06:57.390
Hanamiya Girls' Yotsuba Sayo, 
is starting with Problem A!

00:07:00.390 --> 00:07:02.440
<i>From this thin hold,</i>

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:05.520
<i>I make two moves to that 
easy one and take a rest.</i>

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:08.150
<i>After that, I clip my rope 
to that carabiner...</i>

00:07:08.150 --> 00:07:11.180
Wow. Her movements are so pretty.

00:07:11.180 --> 00:07:12.300
Right?

00:07:12.300 --> 00:07:15.030
She has a clear vision of 
how to solve this problem.

00:07:15.030 --> 00:07:18.790
Yotsuba sends the problem with 
three whole minutes remaining!

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:20.760
The Princess of Lead does it again!

00:07:20.760 --> 00:07:24.090
Was this problem too easy for her?

00:07:25.430 --> 00:07:26.920
That's one down.

00:07:27.600 --> 00:07:29.120
Welcome back, Sayo-chin.

00:07:29.120 --> 00:07:30.170
Well done.

00:07:30.170 --> 00:07:34.680
<i>Wow. Both Nono-san and the 
captain were amazing.</i>

00:07:34.990 --> 00:07:38.680
<i>And I'm on their team.</i>

00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:43.190
<i>I'm gonna go for it, too... I have to!</i>

00:07:43.780 --> 00:07:46.200
<i>I'll be attempting Problem A first.</i>

00:07:46.630 --> 00:07:49.570
<i>I've gotten a decent read 
on most of the holds.</i>

00:07:49.570 --> 00:07:50.680
<i>All that's left is...</i>

00:07:50.680 --> 00:07:51.520
Let me guess.

00:07:51.520 --> 00:07:55.580
You're thinking about how to 
get past that furmidable crux?

00:07:55.580 --> 00:07:59.200
Are you a first-year? Is this 
your first lead competition?

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:00.410
Ah, yes.

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:05.740
Oh, sorry. I'm Uchimura Akane
 from Matsuhashi High.

00:08:05.740 --> 00:08:06.590
And you?

00:08:06.910 --> 00:08:09.020
I'm Kasahara Konomi.

00:08:09.020 --> 00:08:09.960
Konomi-chan, huh?

00:08:10.360 --> 00:08:11.820
It's a pawleasure to meet you!

00:08:11.820 --> 00:08:14.490
So, that crux looks difficult.

00:08:14.980 --> 00:08:19.130
It needs some kind of jump, 
like a lunge or a double dyno.

00:08:19.130 --> 00:08:19.960
Look.

00:08:19.960 --> 00:08:22.560
There's a bunch of chalk on top of that hold.

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:24.730
Looks like we have to get our hands up there.

00:08:24.730 --> 00:08:27.740
<i>You have to jump for that crux?</i>

00:08:27.740 --> 00:08:30.030
<i>But I was thinking...</i>

00:08:30.030 --> 00:08:33.990
Are you feeling a ton of purressure?

00:08:34.500 --> 00:08:40.620
I've seen so many girls wilt 
under it and quit climbing.

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:42.990
If that happened to you,
 it would be a cat-astrophe.

00:08:42.990 --> 00:08:46.250
Let's both do our best to send the problem!

00:08:47.600 --> 00:08:48.700
Yeah!

00:08:49.490 --> 00:08:51.880
Kasahara-san from Hanamiya Girls'?

00:08:52.270 --> 00:08:53.680
Please get ready.

00:08:53.680 --> 00:08:55.160
Oh, okay.

00:08:55.160 --> 00:08:57.280
Thank you, Akane-san.

00:08:57.280 --> 00:09:00.380
Don't mention it. See mew later!

00:09:02.070 --> 00:09:06.400
Next up, making her debut,
 Kasahara Konomi from Hanamiya Girls'!

00:09:06.800 --> 00:09:08.360
<i>It's time.</i>

00:09:08.360 --> 00:09:10.200
Konomin!

00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:10.970
Good luck!

00:09:10.970 --> 00:09:12.390
Konomi-san!

00:09:12.390 --> 00:09:13.680
<i>They're cheering me on!</i>

00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:17.370
<i>I need to live up to their expectations!</i>

00:09:19.790 --> 00:09:24.410
Kasahara's climbing rapidly 
using dynamic moves!

00:09:24.410 --> 00:09:25.750
What's she doing?

00:09:26.750 --> 00:09:29.800
Why is she doing all these jumps?

00:09:29.800 --> 00:09:32.670
Her analytic skills are supposed 
to be her biggest asset.

00:09:33.320 --> 00:09:36.170
She's going to run out of gas like this.

00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:42.270
<i>Is it because I'm in an official competition? 
I can't generate enough power.</i>

00:09:42.270 --> 00:09:47.440
<i>But I'm part of the Hanamiya 
Climbing team, too.</i>

00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:50.190
<i>I can't let a crux, a problem 
like this, beat me!</i>

00:09:50.190 --> 00:09:52.020
What is that idiot thinking?!

00:09:56.310 --> 00:10:00.010
Whoa, Kasahara has fallen!

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:02.780
Hey, what happened to you?

00:10:03.250 --> 00:10:05.540
Are you okay, Konomin?

00:10:05.540 --> 00:10:08.070
You were climbing kinda strange.

00:10:08.790 --> 00:10:12.290
You must've been nervous because 
it's your debut competition.

00:10:12.290 --> 00:10:13.560
That girl...

00:10:13.560 --> 00:10:16.300
It happens! It still happens to me, even!

00:10:18.420 --> 00:10:20.250
Sorry, Jun-chan.

00:10:20.250 --> 00:10:22.440
Huh? Why are you apologizing to me?

00:10:22.440 --> 00:10:25.870
I'm representing the 
Hanamiya Climbing Team...

00:10:25.870 --> 00:10:27.440
Since yesterday, yeah.

00:10:27.440 --> 00:10:28.310
Yeah.

00:10:28.640 --> 00:10:33.000
Hey, did a girl from another school 
put strange ideas in your head?

00:10:33.850 --> 00:10:35.320
The one who speaks in obnoxious cat puns.

00:10:36.920 --> 00:10:38.640
I knew it.

00:10:38.640 --> 00:10:41.950
That jerk's still a disgrace to climbing.

00:10:44.310 --> 00:10:45.450
Sorry.

00:10:45.800 --> 00:10:47.770
You have nothing to apologize for!

00:10:47.770 --> 00:10:52.620
But I'm supposed to be representing 
the amazing Hanamiya team.

00:10:52.620 --> 00:10:54.960
Again, you only joined yesterday.

00:10:54.960 --> 00:11:00.760
That's not it. I just feel 
like maybe I don't belong...

00:11:00.760 --> 00:11:01.720
Konomi!

00:11:01.720 --> 00:11:05.760
By twisting one leg inward,
 you can raise your waist position.

00:11:05.760 --> 00:11:08.980
That gives you a longer reach 
and lets you get to farther holds.

00:11:09.310 --> 00:11:13.560
This is a basic move called 
the Egyptian, or drop knee.

00:11:13.560 --> 00:11:14.480
Egyptian...

00:11:14.910 --> 00:11:17.530
Every hold has a mostly optimal solution,

00:11:17.530 --> 00:11:20.490
and moves are basically climbing formulas.

00:11:20.940 --> 00:11:25.870
Right now, you're trying to solve 
problems without knowing those formulas.

00:11:26.630 --> 00:11:31.120
Just learning the Egyptian should 
help make things easier for you.

00:11:32.180 --> 00:11:36.500
If you have anything to apologize for, 
it's your failure to believe in yourself.

00:11:41.530 --> 00:11:44.640
If you want to be a real climber,
 ignore what others say

00:11:44.640 --> 00:11:46.810
and trust your instincts.

00:11:48.900 --> 00:11:51.300
Thank you, Jun-chan.

00:11:55.400 --> 00:12:00.150
<b>Zonal High School Spring 
Climbing Championships
Practice Wall<b></b></b>

00:11:58.080 --> 00:11:58.880
Nono.

00:11:58.880 --> 00:12:00.150
Shh!

00:12:00.430 --> 00:12:04.110
Yoo-hoo, Konomin! 
I'll buy you a smoothie later...

00:12:04.110 --> 00:12:04.840
Huh?

00:12:04.840 --> 00:12:06.660
Go for a hold that's far out.

00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:09.310
Twisting one leg inward 
raises my waist position.

00:12:09.310 --> 00:12:10.660
Raises my waist position.

00:12:10.660 --> 00:12:13.120
Use that extra reach to 
get to a farther hold.

00:12:13.120 --> 00:12:14.330
Use that extra reach.

00:12:14.640 --> 00:12:16.840
Get to a farther hold.

00:12:16.840 --> 00:12:20.640
See? I told you it would be 
fine if we let Jun handle it.

00:12:20.640 --> 00:12:22.140
Right...

00:12:26.400 --> 00:12:28.350
Woohoo!

00:12:26.760 --> 00:12:28.350
Sugiura sends the problem!

00:12:28.920 --> 00:12:30.720
Yotsuba sends the problem!

00:12:37.480 --> 00:12:40.760
Uchimura falls and fails to clear Problem B!

00:12:40.760 --> 00:12:42.300
Give her a big hand!

00:12:41.440 --> 00:12:43.240
Your cheers are the cat's meow!

00:12:43.880 --> 00:12:48.010
<i>I actually wanted to go 
further, but whatever.</i>

00:12:48.010 --> 00:12:51.500
<i>I'm sure to pass the prelims 
with my combined score.</i>

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:53.480
You haven't changed, huh?

00:12:54.300 --> 00:12:55.740
Uehara Jun!

00:12:55.740 --> 00:12:58.670
You're still trying to drive 
newbies out of the sport?

00:12:58.990 --> 00:13:01.290
Wh-What in the world?

00:13:01.290 --> 00:13:04.190
I have no idea what you could pawsibly mean.

00:13:04.190 --> 00:13:06.240
You're amazing, Akane-chan!

00:13:06.240 --> 00:13:09.550
<i>I'd gotten a big head for being 
a better climber than most</i>

00:13:09.550 --> 00:13:11.530
<i>when a newbie showed up out of nowhere.</i>

00:13:11.930 --> 00:13:16.440
<i>She sent the problem faster than anyone 
else and looked down on the audience.</i>

00:13:16.810 --> 00:13:20.440
<i>She became the star in every 
local competition after that.</i>

00:13:20.440 --> 00:13:23.190
<i>How dare she, when she started after me!</i>

00:13:23.190 --> 00:13:28.450
<i>So, I swore to destroy every 
newbie I came across.</i>

00:13:29.620 --> 00:13:34.110
Anyway, could you please
 go somewhere else?

00:13:34.110 --> 00:13:36.670
I don't have the time to throw 
paws with you right now.

00:13:36.920 --> 00:13:39.510
I just thought this was the 
best seat in the house.

00:13:40.070 --> 00:13:43.760
I wanna get a good look at your face 
after you see our newbie climb.

00:13:44.420 --> 00:13:48.550
Who, that loser who doesn't 
know how to analyze a problem?

00:13:49.760 --> 00:13:53.800
What kind of expurression 
do you want me to make?

00:13:53.800 --> 00:13:57.140
Laugh my tail off?
 Be shocked by how pawful she is?

00:13:57.140 --> 00:14:01.150
I don't know if I can 
act this out purrfectly!

00:14:05.040 --> 00:14:08.530
<i>Yeah, I'm fine. I'm calm and composed.</i>

00:14:08.910 --> 00:14:12.450
<i>Watch me, Captain, Nono-senpai...</i>

00:14:12.930 --> 00:14:14.330
<i>And Jun-chan.</i>

00:14:15.920 --> 00:14:18.340
<i>This is how I climb.</i>

00:14:26.360 --> 00:14:31.770
Whoa, Kasahara's taking it slow and 
steady compared to her previous run.

00:14:31.770 --> 00:14:35.480
Huh... So she's not completely useless.

00:14:35.480 --> 00:14:39.100
But her moves are look like 
something the cat dragged in.

00:14:39.100 --> 00:14:43.730
<i>I have to grab this hold with my left 
hand and get closer to the next one.</i>

00:14:44.060 --> 00:14:47.610
<i>Here, I take a step back to 
safely clip the rope on.</i>

00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:50.520
Konomi-san is using her head now.

00:14:50.520 --> 00:14:53.320
Yeah, she's looking really good.

00:14:53.320 --> 00:14:56.320
But now, she has to deal 
with the slight overhang.

00:14:56.320 --> 00:14:56.910
Yeah.

00:14:56.910 --> 00:15:01.420
Overhangs bring gravity into play more, 
which wears you out quicker.

00:15:01.760 --> 00:15:04.420
She'll run out of gas and fall soon enough.

00:15:06.670 --> 00:15:09.590
<i>This angle sucks!</i>

00:15:09.590 --> 00:15:12.180
<i>My arms can't take any more!</i>

00:15:13.440 --> 00:15:15.680
See? She's just about done fur.

00:15:18.080 --> 00:15:20.310
<i>I know! This is the perfect time!</i>

00:15:23.600 --> 00:15:24.310
The Egyptian?!

00:15:24.570 --> 00:15:27.940
I just taught her that move 
and she's already using it as a rest hold?

00:15:28.440 --> 00:15:31.460
She's secured her lower body 
in place to rest her arms?

00:15:35.590 --> 00:15:38.580
<i>Okay, I can keep going now.</i>

00:15:40.100 --> 00:15:40.960
I knew it.

00:15:41.310 --> 00:15:43.550
That girl really isn't normal.

00:15:43.550 --> 00:15:45.210
This will be fun!

00:15:49.370 --> 00:15:52.720
What the heck? She keeps going, 
like she's done this before.

00:15:52.720 --> 00:15:56.600
Did she get a perfect read on 
the problem as a total newbie?

00:15:56.990 --> 00:16:01.600
<i>I can't move like I envisioned 
when I'm actually climbing.</i>

00:16:01.930 --> 00:16:02.900
<i>But...</i>

00:16:08.560 --> 00:16:09.610
That volume...

00:16:13.420 --> 00:16:15.490
It's the one I fell from.

00:16:16.070 --> 00:16:17.990
<i>Put together a sequence.</i>

00:16:17.990 --> 00:16:21.200
No... She can't get higher than me!

00:16:21.730 --> 00:16:24.210
<i>Fit the pieces together and find a path!</i>

00:16:24.210 --> 00:16:26.210
<i>Send this thing home!</i>

00:16:26.210 --> 00:16:29.590
Gah! I would never lose to her!

00:16:40.220 --> 00:16:43.230
Kasahara grabs hold of the volume.

00:16:43.230 --> 00:16:44.860
No way...

00:16:45.830 --> 00:16:47.400
Love that look, Uchimura.

00:16:50.200 --> 00:16:53.070
I'll let you off the hook for this,

00:16:53.070 --> 00:16:56.260
but the next time you try anything 
funny with us, you'll pay for it.

00:16:57.910 --> 00:16:59.240
Etch this into your tiny brain.

00:16:59.240 --> 00:17:03.160
This is Hanamiya's... 
Kasahara Konomi's brand of climbing.

00:17:05.170 --> 00:17:08.730
<i>The next hold looks simple to grab.</i>

00:17:09.200 --> 00:17:12.470
<i>It's a little far, 
so I should take a step back...</i>

00:17:14.630 --> 00:17:17.130
Oh no! She falls so close to the goal!

00:17:17.130 --> 00:17:19.640
But she showed us an amazing series of moves!

00:17:19.640 --> 00:17:20.970
Give her a big hand!

00:17:21.670 --> 00:17:24.310
Huh? I messed up?

00:17:24.820 --> 00:17:26.390
My hands are shaking...

00:17:29.700 --> 00:17:31.280
You can barely stand.

00:17:31.280 --> 00:17:32.320
Jun-chan.

00:17:32.640 --> 00:17:33.640
Here.

00:17:34.680 --> 00:17:37.640
You lacked the strength to send it, huh?

00:17:37.640 --> 00:17:41.370
Yeah... It didn't go as easily as I imagined.

00:17:42.950 --> 00:17:44.040
But...

00:17:46.580 --> 00:17:51.910
Maybe that's exactly what 
makes you want to go again.

00:17:53.750 --> 00:17:56.970
Get a load of this newbie acting 
like she knows the sport inside out.

00:17:59.780 --> 00:18:01.520
Damn it all!

00:18:01.520 --> 00:18:04.750
What was with that Kasahara Konomi girl?

00:18:04.750 --> 00:18:06.980
She got one hold higher than I did.

00:18:07.410 --> 00:18:09.980
Know your place, damn noob!

00:18:10.450 --> 00:18:13.730
Yeah, I have to destroy every 
rookie I come across immediately.

00:18:14.500 --> 00:18:16.040
My... My neck!

00:18:15.200 --> 00:18:19.160
Bad girl. If you bump into someone,
 you need apologize to them.

00:18:19.700 --> 00:18:22.780
Aren't you Kurikawa High's 
Iwamine? Screw you!

00:18:22.780 --> 00:18:26.620
Not only do you not apologize, 
you're insulting me now? Very bad.

00:18:27.280 --> 00:18:31.000
<i>How is she generating such grip 
strength with just a few fingers?</i>

00:18:32.380 --> 00:18:35.370
I must say, you have a very cute face.

00:18:32.730 --> 00:18:34.250
I can't get free.

00:18:34.250 --> 00:18:35.720
G-Get out of my face.

00:18:35.370 --> 00:18:37.210
Come with me to the dressing rooms.

00:18:37.650 --> 00:18:40.470
I'll give you a good dressing down there.

00:18:41.390 --> 00:18:43.800
Wait! Let me go!

00:18:43.800 --> 00:18:46.470
I-I'm sorry, Iwamine-san!

00:18:46.470 --> 00:18:49.520
I was wrong! Spare me!

00:18:49.520 --> 00:18:53.110
No!

00:18:55.530 --> 00:18:57.070
We did it!

00:18:57.070 --> 00:19:00.160
The Hanamiya Climbing Team takes 
home the honors again this year!

00:19:00.480 --> 00:19:03.260
And, this time, 
we're individual <i>and</i> team champions.

00:19:03.260 --> 00:19:06.040
Hell yeah! We finally won as a team!

00:19:06.330 --> 00:19:08.250
<i>It was amazing.</i>

00:19:08.250 --> 00:19:12.300
<i>Captain, Jun-chan, and Nono-san 
all finished on the podium.</i>

00:19:12.790 --> 00:19:16.030
<i>I didn't even make the finals.</i>

00:19:16.030 --> 00:19:17.640
Now, Konomi-san.

00:19:18.450 --> 00:19:21.780
I want to ask you: Do you want to continue?

00:19:22.480 --> 00:19:26.060
I would like to know how 
you really feel right now.

00:19:26.060 --> 00:19:27.370
I...

00:19:27.370 --> 00:19:30.920
Our goal is to make Hanamiya 
national champions.

00:19:31.910 --> 00:19:35.800
I want us to be the best team in Japan.

00:19:35.800 --> 00:19:39.070
And, using that as a springboard, 
I'll enter international competitions,

00:19:39.390 --> 00:19:43.700
win lots of medals, and help spread the 
sport of climbing across the globe.

00:19:44.880 --> 00:19:48.580
That will make walls a 
more commonplace thing.

00:19:48.580 --> 00:19:52.580
They will be everywhere, 
including schools and streets.

00:19:52.580 --> 00:19:56.840
I'll bring to fruition a world where everyone, 
everywhere, can climb all they want!

00:19:54.440 --> 00:19:56.230
Not again, Sayo-chin...

00:19:57.280 --> 00:20:00.550
That is my dream!

00:20:02.660 --> 00:20:03.660
Your dream...

00:20:05.190 --> 00:20:06.430
I love it.

00:20:06.430 --> 00:20:07.810
Isn't it the best?

00:20:08.240 --> 00:20:10.810
Hey, Sayo-chin! 
Konomin's eyes are glazing over!

00:20:15.590 --> 00:20:19.500
Of course, becoming national 
champions will be no mean feat.

00:20:19.500 --> 00:20:23.740
Our generation is filled with talent thanks to 
development at the junior level.

00:20:24.170 --> 00:20:26.890
There are several competitors better than me.

00:20:27.540 --> 00:20:29.870
Iwamine Chinari, the Climbing Spider.

00:20:30.290 --> 00:20:32.870
Kumagai Chigusa, the Muscle Maxima'am.

00:20:33.640 --> 00:20:35.880
Fujita Masumi, the Black Panther.

00:20:36.400 --> 00:20:38.880
Samura Rina, the Crimson Stormtrooper.

00:20:39.350 --> 00:20:41.880
Ooba Kurea, the Ballerina of Rock.

00:20:42.310 --> 00:20:45.420
And the Princess of Climbing, Kurusu Anne!

00:20:45.420 --> 00:20:47.390
Cool Kurusu!

00:20:47.690 --> 00:20:51.000
Konomi-san, you have real talent for this.

00:20:51.000 --> 00:20:55.900
We'll need your talent if we wish to 
win competitions bigger than today's.

00:20:58.840 --> 00:21:02.780
Would you be willing to scale 
the national wall with us?

00:21:04.930 --> 00:21:06.200
I...

00:21:07.920 --> 00:21:10.800
I know I'm sorely lacking in experience.

00:21:10.800 --> 00:21:11.410
However,

00:21:11.730 --> 00:21:17.900
I know how good the view from the top can be.

00:21:19.240 --> 00:21:22.670
I would love to see that 
view together with you all!

00:21:24.600 --> 00:21:27.300
I have a lot to learn,
 but thanks for having me!

00:21:27.300 --> 00:21:31.700
I'll do my best to bring 
home that chicken dinner!

00:21:35.350 --> 00:21:36.180
Er...

00:21:36.680 --> 00:21:40.110
Konomi-san? "Chicken dinner"?

00:21:40.410 --> 00:21:44.400
Oh, uh, "winner, winner, 
chicken dinner," gamer lingo.

00:21:44.400 --> 00:21:46.610
The national championship, in this case.

00:21:47.010 --> 00:21:48.960
Huh, I had no idea.

00:21:48.960 --> 00:21:50.760
Sorry, old habits.

00:21:51.560 --> 00:21:53.530
What's the matter, Jun?

00:21:53.530 --> 00:21:55.370
Huh? Oh, nothing.

00:21:55.710 --> 00:21:56.670
Really?

00:21:56.670 --> 00:21:58.700
Let's all say it together, then.

00:21:58.700 --> 00:21:59.390
Huh?

00:21:59.390 --> 00:22:00.160
Say what?

00:22:00.160 --> 00:22:01.250
Together?

00:22:02.100 --> 00:22:03.580
Chicken dinner!

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:39.980
<b><i>Iwakakeru!</i></b>

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:39.980
<b><i>Wall 3: The Anti-Monkey Rock</i></b>
